<HelpTab>
    <HelpSection Title="Notifications are blocked">
        <FluentText>
            If you chose <strong>Don't Allow</strong> earlier, your phone won't ask again. Allow them yourself, then
            come back to Get Started and select <strong>Check again</strong>:
        </FluentText>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>iPhone and iPad:</strong> Settings › Notifications, pick the app, then turn on Allow Notifications.</li>
            <li><strong>Android:</strong> long-press the app icon, choose App info › Notifications, and turn them on.</li>
            <li><strong>Computer:</strong> click the icon beside the address bar, open the site settings and allow notifications.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="The test didn't arrive">
        <ul>
            <li>Check Do Not Disturb or Focus is off.</li>
            <li>Battery saver can hold notifications back - try with it off.</li>
            <li>Some phones bundle notifications together, so give it a minute.</li>
            <li>Still nothing? In Account Management, turn notifications off and on again for this device.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="No notifications option on iPhone">
        <FluentText>
            iPhones and iPads need iOS 16.4 or later, and Lanyard has to be opened from the Home Screen rather than
            Safari. Update your phone in Settings › General › Software Update if Get Started says it's too old.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
